.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All commits applied successfully (or dry-run completed).
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred: invalid arguments, git failures, unresolvable
conflicts, build failures, or missing prerequisites.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .backport/session.json
Automatic session file storing parameters and metadata.
.TP
.I .backport\-dist\-configs\-head
Stamp file in the RHEL repo tracking the HEAD hash for
.B dist-configs
caching.
.TP
.I <output\-dir>/state.json
Saved state for
.B continue
resumption.
.TP
.I <isb\-install\-dir>/api\-replacements.json
Baseline API replacement rules shipped with
.BR isb .
Contains upstream\-to\-RHEL API symbol mappings used for
Phase\ 3 commit filtering (omitting commits that use
APIs absent from RHEL) and build\-time auto\-fix (rewriting
upstream\-only calls like
.BR kzalloc_obj ()
to RHEL\-compatible equivalents).
Do not edit this file; it is updated with each
.B isb
release.
.TP
.I ~/.config/isb/api\-replacements.json
Optional per\-user override.
Entries here are merged on top of the baseline: new symbols
are added and existing symbols are overridden.
Use this to add replacement rules for new upstream API
conversions without modifying the shipped config.
The format is identical to the baseline file.
.SH "TOOLBOX PATH RULES"
Toolbox bind\-mounts
.B $HOME
into the container.
Host paths outside
.B $HOME
are reached via the host\-root prefix
.B /run/host
concatenated with the absolute path
(for example
.IR /run/host/data/... ).
.B isb
resolves the RHEL repository with
.BR realpath (3)
and syncs the
.B PWD
environment variable to that path before every
.BR "toolbox run" ,
because toolbox follows
.B PWD
rather than the process cwd.
.PP
If the repository realpath is under
.B $HOME
(including when the user entered via a symlink such as
.I /work
\(->
.IR ~/work ),
builds use a normal
.B toolbox run
with cwd and
.B PWD
set to the realpath under
.BR $HOME .
.PP
If the repository realpath is outside
.B $HOME
(for example
.IR /data/... ),
.B isb
wraps the build as
.B toolbox run
plus
.B cd
to the matching
.B /run/host
path inside the container.
.PP
Custom toolboxes without a
.B /run/host
mount, or paths the container cannot see, are not supported;
bind\-mount the tree explicitly or keep the repository under
.BR $HOME .
Path or mount failures are treated as infrastructure errors
and the AI build\-fix loop is skipped.
